# task-queue-pg2-ecosystem

Epic: Project Graph (ADR-0032; mnemo decisions 266aa582, 8457c635, 3359b0f8; releases 5.1.0/5.1.1 shipped).

DELIVERABLE: ecosystem instrumentation around the project graph.
- vitals metrics: staleness-%, tokens-per-session (graph vs no-graph), hit-rate of the shared index, index degradation as a metric;
- eyes subsections (ONE schema; sample aggregates keyed by session_id WITHOUT node content): Projects (drilldown / blast-radius / diff), Sessions (timeline), Agents (swarm view), Tasks (stitching of task contexts); TOTP on remote (ADR-0014); read-audit of views;
- wire audit -> vitals (accepted deviation (v) of the PR #438 review is the gate of this wave);
- beacon display counter;
- GCW skill for consumption = OPTIONAL polish only (native consumption already works without it).

OWNER: gcw-product-architect (lead: metrics + subsection design), implementation dispatched to gcw-senior-system-engineer at execution. Single owner tag = architect.
GATE: PG-1 (task-queue-pg1-recall-repo-map) green AND S5 run "with graph vs without" done.
Size: L — split at dispatch. Priority: P2.
